    "updated_at": "2025-04-30T09:31:43Z",
    "body": "Upon further consideration I think supporting `[AllowResizable]` for all of these is reasonable. The weirdest thing that could happen is that `encodeInto()` returns numbers that are no longer accurate because the buffer grew, but that would only happen in some kind of race with the `encodeInto()` call, at which point that's to be expected.\n\nAnd yes, the specification will continue to define this as doing a copy that could potentially be elided with a lot of careful work.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
